+// SetRandomizedElectionTimeout sets the randomized election timeout of this
+// node to the given value, overriding the value that would otherwise be drawn
+// from the random source (see Config.ElectionTimeoutRand). The value must lie
+// in [ElectionTick, 2*ElectionTick-1]; like the internal draw it replaces,
+// values outside this range are accepted verbatim and make elections fire
+// proportionally earlier or later.
+//
+// The randomized election timeout is re-drawn whenever the node becomes a
+// follower, candidate, or leader, so tests that need determinism across those
+// transitions should either supply Config.ElectionTimeoutRand or re-apply this
+// method after each transition.
+func (rn *RawNode) SetRandomizedElectionTimeout(timeout int) {
+	rn.raft.randomizedElectionTimeout = timeout
+}
